CHECK bb14.1 TRUE in unweighted fits a search is a pair search exactly when A >= 0.01 (1966 searches; bracket 0.00950996, 0.0107171)
CHECK bb14.2 TRUE 1 - R^2 of b*x does not decide the kind: single-hinge searches reach 0.507 and pair searches go down to 0.00115
CHECK bb14.3 TRUE at a fixed 1 - R^2, rescaling x2 moves A from 0.009900 to 0.010100 and the search from single-hinge to pair
CHECK bb14.4 TRUE the same data with x and with x / 100 give different models, beyond the scaling of the knots
CHECK bb14.5 TRUE in a single-hinge search the RSS of a knot is RSS(current columns + h), without b*x
CHECK bb14.6 TRUE in a single-hinge search a knot at a repeated minimum can pass the collinearity test (TolG 1)
CHECK bb14.7 TRUE with weights that are not all equal, earth runs pair searches below A = 0.01
